{"name":"Casting Shadow","hex":"#9da7a0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"casting","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of cast"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or process of selecting actors, singers, dancers, models, etc.","A manufacturing process using a mold."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casting"},{"term":"shadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark image projected onto a surface where light (or other radiation) is blocked by the shade of an object.","Relative darkness, especially as caused by the interruption of light; gloom; obscurity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unofficial, informal, unauthorized, but acting as though it were.","Having power or influence, but not widely known or recognized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Casting","blocks":[{"text":"Casting is a manufacturing process in which a liquid material is usually poured into a mold, which contains a hollow cavity of the desired shape, and then allowed to solidify. The solidified part is also known as a casting, which is ejected or broken out of the mold to complete the process. Casting materials are usually metals or various time setting materials that cure after mixing two or more components together; examples are epoxy, concrete, plaster and clay. Casting is most often used for making complex shapes that would be otherwise difficult or uneconomical to make by other methods. Heavy equipment like machine tool beds, ships' propellers, etc. can be cast easily in the required size, rather than fabricating by joining several small pieces. Casting is a 7,000-year-old process. The oldest surviving casting is a copper frog from 3200 BC."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Cast_iron_melting.JPG/330px-Cast_iron_melting.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casting","wikidata":"Q496098"},{"title":"Shadow","blocks":[{"text":"A shadow is a dark area on a surface where light from a light source is blocked by an object. In contrast, shade occupies the three-dimensional volume behind an object with light in front of it. The cross-section of a shadow is a two-dimensional silhouette, or a reverse projection of the object blocking the light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg/330px-The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow","wikidata":"Q160020"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Dancing_girl_of_Mohenjo-daro.jpg/500px-Dancing_girl_of_Mohenjo-daro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Dancing_girl_of_Mohenjo-daro.jpg/1280px-Dancing_girl_of_Mohenjo-daro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Dancing_girl_of_Mohenjo-daro.jpg/500px-Dancing_girl_of_Mohenjo-daro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dancing girl of Mohenjo-daro","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADancing_girl_of_Mohenjo-daro.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Casting.jpg/330px-Casting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Casting.jpg/330px-Casting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Judenplatz Holocaust Memorial (Nameless Library), by Rachel Whiteread. Concrete cast of books on library shelves turned inside out.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACasting.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Poligonsoft_casting.jpg/500px-Poligonsoft_casting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Poligonsoft_casting.jpg/500px-Poligonsoft_casting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A high-performance software for the simulation of casting processes provides opportunities for an interactive or automated evaluation of results (here, for example, of mold filling and solidification, porosity and flow characteristics).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APoligonsoft_casting.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Park_grid.JPG/500px-Park_grid.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Park_grid.JPG/1280px-Park_grid.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Park_grid.JPG/500px-Park_grid.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Park fence shadow is distorted by an uneven snow surface.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APark_grid.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cumulus_cloud_shadows_1.jpg/500px-Cumulus_cloud_shadows_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cumulus_cloud_shadows_1.jpg/1280px-Cumulus_cloud_shadows_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cumulus_cloud_shadows_1.jpg/500px-Cumulus_cloud_shadows_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shadows from cumulus clouds thick enough to bloc